column1:
Fix the race condition in the following Go code. The Counter struct has Increment and Get methods but they are not thread-safe — the sync.Mutex field is declared but never used. Fix the mutex usage so both methods are protected. Verify with go build -race:

type Counter struct {
    mu    sync.Mutex
    value int
}

func (c *Counter) Increment() {
    c.value++
}

func (c *Counter) Get() int {
    return c.value
}

Write a Go Validate method for the following User struct that checks: Name is not empty, Email contains exactly one '@' character, Age is between 0 and 150. Return a descriptive error for each violation:

type User struct {
    Name  string
    Email string
    Age   int
}

Fix the race condition in the following Go code. The Cache struct has Set and Get methods but neither acquires the mutex. Fix the sync.RWMutex usage so Set uses Lock/Unlock and Get uses RLock/RUnlock:

type Cache struct {
    mu    sync.RWMutex
    store map[string]string
}

func (c *Cache) Set(key, value string) {
    c.store[key] = value
}

func (c *Cache) Get(key string) (string, bool) {
    v, ok := c.store[key]
    return v, ok
}

Write a Go Validate method for the following Product struct that checks: Title is not empty, Price is strictly greater than 0, SKU matches the pattern [A-Z]{3}-[0-9]{4}. Return a descriptive error for each violation:

type Product struct {
    Title string
    Price float64
    SKU   string
}

There is a concurrency bug in the following Go code. The WorkerPool has a counter field that is incremented by multiple goroutines without synchronization. Add sync/atomic operations (atomic.AddInt64) to make the counter thread-safe. Also add a Done method that returns the current count safely:

type WorkerPool struct {
    counter int64
    wg      sync.WaitGroup
}

func (wp *WorkerPool) Add() {
    wp.counter++
}

Write a Go Validate method for the following Order struct that checks: CustomerID is not zero, Items slice is not empty, each Item has Quantity > 0 and UnitPrice >= 0, TotalAmount equals the sum of all Item.Quantity * Item.UnitPrice. Return all validation errors concatenated:

type Order struct {
    CustomerID  int
    Items       []OrderItem
    TotalAmount float64
}

type OrderItem struct {
    ProductID int
    Quantity  int
    UnitPrice float64
}
